234	Each displayed construction estimate below has its own universal constant $C_E \geq 1$, quantified independently, and its own scale $\delta_P^E=C_EB$. The source uses one enlarged error $\delta_S$ for all of these estimates. The two presentations agree: after the finitely many estimates have been established, take $C_* = \max_E C_E$ and $\delta_P=C_*B$. Since $B\geq0$, every bound remains valid at this common scale. In the proof paragraphs, $\delta_P$ denotes this common enlargement. It has the same asymptotic form as $\delta_G$: after shrinking $b$ to at most $1/2$, the term $\eps^b$ dominates $\sqrt{\eps}$ for $0 \leq \eps \leq 1$, while $(md)^a q^{-b}$ dominates $md/q$.
